      "How GST on freight works, stated as of September 2026. GST on goods transport agency services can be charged by the transporter under forward charge or paid by the shipper under reverse charge, depending on the status of both parties. A GST-registered GTA can charge 5% on freight without passing on input tax credit or 12% with input tax credit, and the option chosen must be stated on the invoice. The registration threshold for goods transport agencies is 40 lakh rupees of aggregate turnover in most states and 20 lakh rupees in special-category states. Whatever route applies to you, only a registered transporter's invoice carries the GSTIN that either route needs.",
